Digest ( username , password )
>> Server sends a nonce (one-time code), client responds with a hashed value of credentials + nonce.
>> More secure than Basic Auth.
>> It’s an authentication mechanism where:
   Client requests a resource.
   Server responds with a nonce (random one-time-use number) + auth challenge.
   Client hashes (encrypts) -> the username, password, nonce, HTTP method, and URI.
   Server verifies the hashed response to authenticate the client.
>> given()
       .auth().digest("user", "pass")  // Handles nonce automatically
   .when()
       .get("https://api.example.com/digest-auth");
