Basic Auth ( username , password ) Base64
>> Credentials sent as username:password encoded in Base64 in the Authorization header.
>> It’s an authentication mechanism where:
   Client requests a resource by sending username and password encoded in Base64 along with the request header.
   Server decodes the Base64 string to retrieve credentials.
   Server validates the username and password against its stored records.
   If correct, access is granted; else, access is denied.
>> // Preemptive (always sends credentials)
given()
    .auth().preemptive().basic("user", "pass")
.when()
    .get("https://api.example.com/secure");

// Challenged (waits for 401)
given()
    .auth().basic("user", "pass")  // Only sends if challenged
