OAuth 1.0
>> Uses consumerKey, consumerSecret, accessToken, and tokenSecret to sign requests.
given()
    .auth().oauth(
        "consumerKey", "consumerSecret",
        "accessToken", "tokenSecret")  // Signs the request
.when()
    .get("https://api.example.com/oauth1");
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OAuth 2.0
>> Simpler than OAuth 1.0. Uses access_token (often JWT).
// Client Credentials Flow (auto-fetch token):
String token = given()
    .params(
        "grant_type", "client_credentials",
        "client_id", "id",
        "client_secret", "secret")
.when()
    .post("https://auth.server.com/token")
.then()
    .extract().path("access_token");

given()
    .auth().oauth2(token);  // Use the fetched token
